{
  "format": "lplscene/1",
  "_comment": "The world the kernel's graphical profile draws. Baked to world.lplpak and carried in the ISO as a second GRUB module, ALONGSIDE game.lplpak \u2014 which stays the parity gate's cartridge. Two modules rather than one because the gate folds what it boots: giving it this scene instead would change the folded world and compare the kernel against an oracle that baked something else.",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Laplace World Viewer",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "profile": "solo",
    "startScene": "overworld",
    "online": false,
    "minPlayers": 1,
    "maxPlayers": 1,
    "maxInstances": 1
  },
  "scenes": [
    {
      "name": "overworld",
      "systems": [
        "position",
        "handleCollision",
        "rigid_body",
        "render"
      ],
      "resources": [],
      "_procedural_comment": "Sized for the kernel: 64x64 is ~8000 triangles a frame in the software rasterizer and a few hundred kilobytes of grids on a 4 MiB heap. Everything else is turned UP relative to the parity recipe, because this one exists to be looked at rather than folded \u2014 a town, a road network, caves and a scatter dense enough to read as vegetation.",
      "procedural": {
        "seed": 20260728,
        "width": 64,
        "depth": 64,
        "cellSize": 1.0,
        "terrain": {
          "seed": 20260728,
          "frequency": 0.09,
